                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c31eb016-3fb4-37a0-acdd-3640ae5f1fb7",
                        "entry_id": "9151af2b-5b28-3cd7-bfc5-b2ca6474728a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fossil plant resembling a petrified flower."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d27083d5-4802-46c3-8852-ca0cf29e5866",
                                "sense_id": "c31eb016-3fb4-37a0-acdd-3640ae5f1fb7",
                                "text": "He considers this Antholite from the coal to be \"the spike of a very highly organised flowering plant in full flower,\", p. 20."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1eb41775-da4e-4eb9-8fb1-7f503ca5b764",
                                "sense_id": "c31eb016-3fb4-37a0-acdd-3640ae5f1fb7",
                                "text": "Göppert , in his Permian Flora , figures an Antholite (pl. xxi., fig. 1-3), which he considers to be teh inflorescence of Nöggerathia, a genus placed by him among the monocotyledons; while Ettingshausen, on the other hand, believes teh forms he found in the Coal-Measures at Stradonitz to be the fruits of Calamites (\"Steinkohlenflora Stradonitz,\" pl. v. fig. 1-3)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9640f78e-c86b-4d39-99bc-e970403a3943",
                                "sense_id": "c31eb016-3fb4-37a0-acdd-3640ae5f1fb7",
                                "text": "It is not, as you have perhaps surmised, a work of sculpture, but it is an antholite, or fossil blossom, brought, with others of the same kind, from the world to which I am native."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bca2a8c3-c295-363c-860d-26b6d4c0133b",
                        "entry_id": "9151af2b-5b28-3cd7-bfc5-b2ca6474728a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fibrous form of amphibole."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a94e730-8e75-4289-b78b-99b9964c3c32",
                                "sense_id": "bca2a8c3-c295-363c-860d-26b6d4c0133b",
                                "text": "Antholite is fibrous or asbestiform, grey to brown; […] Cummingtonite is much like antholite, gey to brown; fibrous;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "674df028-7f3e-4c1a-9266-5ba5315abd8d",
                                "sense_id": "bca2a8c3-c295-363c-860d-26b6d4c0133b",
                                "text": "In thin section, the radiated variety of amphibole, antholite ( possibly true anthophyllite ) , predominates in closely matted groups, made up of colorless to brownish ( ochreous ) fibres, which polarize strongly between the crossed nicols."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a195b2e-4ec0-4cc5-bb4b-70b23c0e3a7d",
                                "sense_id": "bca2a8c3-c295-363c-860d-26b6d4c0133b",
                                "text": "It seems to correspond most nearly in chemical composition to some of the fibrous forms of monoclinic amphibole, e.g. antholite or kuppferite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe246785-4ac2-4bdd-9db3-b6a2981bde5b",
                                "sense_id": "bca2a8c3-c295-363c-860d-26b6d4c0133b",
                                "text": "Antholite is found in irregular bundles of strong fibres associated with altered enstatite, calcite, dolomite etc"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
